# `bind-read-above`: a block is one binding group (Semantics ch. 4: "any line may use any
# name the block binds"), so a `for` above the bind of the map it runs over is checked with
# that map's type. The checker checks a block's lines other than holds, `let`s and local
# functions in their dependency order, so `$each` is known when the `for` is checked (pick
# BG; gap DG).
emit Ui.*
use Ui.*

@main: @unit
@main:
    !go <- Ui.Button(label=$"go")
    for k, $$d <- $each:
        $v <- @Flatten $$d
        Ui.Label(text=$v)
    $m <- {0: "a"} then $m on !go
    $each <- @PerKey $m
